From: dardiao <xn--6s1a@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 01:41:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] local: signup usernames are subdomains registered on
 the dns platform

The username field now shows a fixed, grey `.niuma.club` suffix and holds only the prefix;
on blur the page verifies that the subdomain really exists on the operator's platform.

The browser cannot call that platform directly (its CORS allowlist only covers its own pages),
so a small same-origin proxy in the ui server does the lookup: /domain-check?name=<prefix>
forwards to https://hapdns.com/api/v1/check. The name is validated against the actor-name
charset before it is used, so the endpoint cannot be pointed at anything else.

Only status "registered" is accepted. "unregistered" (including reserved prefixes, which the
platform reports with a reason) and malformed names block the submit; a lookup failure only
warns, because registration is reviewed by an admin anyway. Input is lower-cased and a pasted
".niuma.club" suffix is stripped, and hyphens are refused up front since Lemmy usernames do not
allow them even though DNS labels do.
